From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:01:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a canvas says the scale its surface box is in

`ExternalSurfaceEmbedder::Embed` takes the page's layout zoom factor now,
so the producer can bring an `<app>`'s box in device pixels back to the
logical pixels a client is configured in. A desk of several monitors is
several pages, each at its own monitor's scale, and the compositor had
been dividing every box by whichever page last reported its ratio.

The spike's canvas embeds through the same call and says its own frame's
factor, which is what it is drawn at.
---
 .../blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/html_canvas_element.cc      | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/html_canvas_element.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/html_canvas_element.cc
index 501590f7ec..47847fe714 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/html_canvas_element.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/html_canvas_element.cc
@@ -2174,7 +2174,7 @@ ScriptPromise<IDLUndefined> HTMLCanvasElement::embedExternalSurface(
   external_surface_embedder_->Embed(
       app_id,
       frame->GetPage()->GetChromeClient().GetFrameSinkId(frame),
-      ExternalSurfaceSize(),
+      ExternalSurfaceSize(), frame->LayoutZoomFactor(),
       reconfiguring ? ExternalSurfaceEmbedder::Allocation::kReconfigure
                     : ExternalSurfaceEmbedder::Allocation::kAdopt,
       BindOnce(&HTMLCanvasElement::OnExternalSurfaceEmbedded,
